  "body": "Part of #785. Split from it: #785's PR posts **indexed** A work only, and refuses an A that changes inside an operation by name (\"simultaneous 4-axis motion ... not confirmed on PathPilot\").\n\n**What's open** (see the answers on #785):\n- Does PathPilot's microARC 4 configuration wrap A (rollover), or treat it as linear degrees? The Tormach guides (TD10749, TD10552, TD10374) don't say, and LinuxCNC leaves it to each machine's configuration.\n- Feed for a combined XYZA move. Under LinuxCNC G94, F is the XYZ feed and A is carried along; G93 inverse time is listed in Tormach's post guidelines. Which should the post write, and does it read as expected on PathPilot?\n\n**Work:**\n- Settle both in the PathPilot Hub, then on the contributor's 770MX with a microARC 4.\n- Then post wrapped A milling (the Rotary Parallel / Contour kinds on an A about X) in `assets/posts/tormach.cps`, with its feed mode.\n- Add the continuous op to the tester kit `docs/tester-kits/tormach-microarc-4th/`. Today its refusal is pinned by `a_wrapped_op_on_the_test_part_is_refused_by_name`.\n\nEffort: high, under the safety floor (it changes posted G-code).\n\n**Done means:** a wrapped op on the 770MX + microARC 4 posts with a confirmed feed mode and rollover handling, pinned by a golden, and is cut on the hardware.\n",
